module

public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Lyons.Atlas111InvolutionLocalCommutant.Words.Data

/-!
# Packed candidates for the local cyclic basis

Q has the binary word orbit as its columns. The other candidates are its
right inverse and its left translates by the two generators.

Source: the literal ATLAS local words and matrices; attribution in
`Atlas111Source/` and `Atlas111InvolutionSource/`. Reproduce these candidates
with `Cyclic/source/Generate.py`. All numerical checks use the Lean kernel.
-/

namespace Lyons.SimplicityCertificate.LocalCommutant.Cyclic

